## SS 10b. Create Regular Post with Image Attached

Same as SS 10 but inserts a media-upload stage between editor open and Post click. Use when `linkedin-post-image.spec.json` exists alongside today's `linkedin-post.md`.

### Step 0: Render spec to PNG

```bash
mkdir -p /tmp/opentwins-uploads
SPEC={{pipeline_workspace}}/content-ready/{today}/linkedin-post-image.spec.json
LAYOUT=$(jq -r .type "$SPEC")
node {{pipeline_workspace}}/image-core/cli.mjs render \
  --platform linkedin --layout "$LAYOUT" \
  --data "$SPEC" \
  --out /tmp/opentwins-uploads/linkedin-post-image.png
```

🚨 If render exits non-zero, skip image stage and fall through to SS 10 (text-only). Never block the post.

### Step 1: Open modal (SS 8, 4s wait)
### Step 2: Type post text (SS 10 Step 2), wait 1s

### Step 3: Click More, then "Add media" (shadow DOM)

```bash
exec curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3847/api/browser/{{browser_profile}}/evaluate -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d @- <<'ENDJSON'
{"fn":"async () => { var shadow = document.querySelector('#interop-outlet').shadowRoot; var moreBtn = Array.from(shadow.querySelectorAll('button')).find(function(b) { return b.getAttribute('aria-label') === 'More'; }); if (!moreBtn) return { success: false, reason: 'no-more-button' }; moreBtn.click(); await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 1000)); var mediaBtn = Array.from(shadow.querySelectorAll('button')).find(function(b) { return b.getAttribute('aria-label') === 'Add media'; }); if (!mediaBtn) return { success: false, reason: 'no-add-media' }; mediaBtn.click(); await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 2000)); return { success: true }; }"}
ENDJSON
```

### Step 4: Direct-set file via selector-mode upload

🚨 **MUST use `selector`.** Intercept mode fires the chooser twice → "1 of 2" duplicate. Selector sets files directly, no chooser.

```bash
curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3847/api/browser/{{browser_profile}}/upload -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"filePath":"/tmp/opentwins-uploads/linkedin-post-image.png","selector":"#media-editor-file-selector__file-input","timeoutMs":10000}'
```

Wait 3s. Editor opens with "1 of 1".

### Step 5: Click "Next" in Editor dialog, wait 2s

```bash
exec curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3847/api/browser/{{browser_profile}}/evaluate -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d @- <<'ENDJSON'
{"fn":"async () => { function walk(root, pred, depth) { depth = depth || 0; if (depth > 6) return null; var hit = Array.from(root.querySelectorAll('*')).find(pred); if (hit) return hit; var hosts = Array.from(root.querySelectorAll('*')).filter(function(el) { return el.shadowRoot; }); for (var i = 0; i < hosts.length; i++) { var r = walk(hosts[i].shadowRoot, pred, depth + 1); if (r) return r; } return null; } var next = walk(document, function(el) { return el.tagName === 'BUTTON' && el.getAttribute('aria-label') === 'Next'; }); if (!next) return { success: false, reason: 'no-next' }; next.click(); await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 2500)); return { success: true }; }"}
ENDJSON
```

### Step 6: Click "Post" (SS 9 Step 9)
### Step 7: Dismiss + verify (SS 9 Step 10)

🚨 **Failure recovery:** if any step 3-5 fails, click Dismiss on the Editor modal (if open), then fall through to SS 10 Step 3 (post text-only). Log as `Post Published` with `image: false`.

